(:id "port/python/vt/text-form/hand-text" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/handtext_test.go: TestPythonHandtextCorpus, TestPythonHandtextUnbounded, TestPythonHandtextNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/pythontable/handtext_test.go: TestPythonHandtextKindArrays, TestPythonHandtextKindsNegativeControl, TestPythonHandtextArrayRoot, TestPythonHandtextArrayRootNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/pythontable/handtext_test.go: TestPythonHandtextWireCarrier, TestPythonHandtextWireCarrierNegativeControl, TestPythonHandtextWireCarrierCRC, TestPythonHandtextWireCarrierCRCNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/pythontable/handtext_test.go: TestPythonHandtextUnionBlobs, TestPythonHandtextUnionBlobsNegativeControl, TestPythonHandtextEditPathNegativeControl, TestPythonHandtextCombinedEditNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/pythontable/handtext_reference_test.go: TestPythonHandtextGoCorpusFunctional, TestPythonHandtextCppCorpusFunctional, TestPythonHandtextUnboundedReferencesFunctional, TestPythonHandtextFixedCarrierCRCFunctional" "make python-handtext, python-handtext-negative-control (make/python-handtext.mk)" "make table-base64-python, table-base64-python-negative-control (make/python-handtext.mk)") :tested-revision "2ec04643b3e871ee70859e615fbda85d76395e13" :note "2026-11-17: the hand-editable text form of SPEC-TABLES §16.9 for every table and field kind the descriptors carry: the four positive documents (roadmap, layout, kinds, variable) read, rewrite byte-identical and edit locally, the unbounded text-list and map-key vectors round-trip, and all 24 refusal vectors answer their stable reason by name, on both fixed and variable roots. The Go and C++ reference comparisons read the same source through their own text forms and agree byte for byte on canonical JSON, and the base64 text channel passes 990 cases per pinned interpreter with padding, refusal and canonical-writer checks. Every negative control plants its fault in a copy of the generated textform runtime or the JSON/base64 runtime and goes red by name. Ran on Linux x86-64 with SCHEMA_SLOW=1 under the pinned CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 interpreters built by make dist-python, at the revision named here, whose code this overlay's own commit leaves unchanged.")
